        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c745dd1a4c9c86f0b776",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 15,
      "hadithIndex": 1362,
      "bookHadithIndex": 42,
      "text": "Narrated Al-Bara':\"My maternal uncle Abu Burdah Ibn Niyar passed by me and he had a flag with him. I said: 'Where are you going ?' He said: 'the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) dispatched me to a man who married a woman his father had married to: that I should bring him his head",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-15-1362-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-15-1362-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-15-1362-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c745dd1a4c9c86f0b777",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 15,
      "hadithIndex": 1363,
      "bookHadithIndex": 43,
      "text": "Narrated 'Abdullah bin Az-Zubair:\"A man from the Ansar disputed with Az-Zubair before the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) about the canals of Harrah which they used to irrigate the date palms. The Ansari said: 'Let the water pass'. But he refused, So they brought their dispute to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ). The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said to Az-Zubair: 'O Zubair! Irrigate (your land) then let the water pass to you neighbor.' The Ansari became angry and said:'[O Messenger of Allah!] Is this because he is your aunt's son?' The face of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) changed color. Then he said: 'O Zubair! Irrigate (your land) and then withhold the water until it reaches the walls.' Az-Zubair said: 'By Allah! I think that this Ayah was revealed about that: But no, by your Lord, they can have no Faith until they make you (O Muhammad) judge in all disputes between them, and find in themselves no resistance against your decisions and accept (them) with full submission",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-15-1363-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-15-1363-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-15-1363-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih - Agreed Upon"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c745dd1a4c9c86f0b778",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 15,
      "hadithIndex": 1364,
      "bookHadithIndex": 44,
      "text": "Narrated 'Imran bin Husain:\"A Man from the Ansar freed six slaves of his upon his death, and he did not have any wealth aside from them. That was conveyed to the Prophet (ﷺ), and he said some harsh words about him.\" He said: \"Then he called for them and he divided them and had them draw lots. So he freed two of them and left four as slaves",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-15-1364-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-15-1364-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-15-1364-basharawadmaarouf",
          "name": "Bashar Awad Maarouf",
          "grade": "Hasan Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-15-1364-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih Muslim"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c745dd1a4c9c86f0b779",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 15,
      "hadithIndex": 1365,
      "bookHadithIndex": 45,
      "text": "",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-15-1365-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-15-1365-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-15-1365-basharawadmaarouf",
          "name": "Bashar Awad Maarouf",
          "grade": "Hasan"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c745dd1a4c9c86f0b77a",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 15,
      "hadithIndex": 1366,
      "bookHadithIndex": 47,
      "text": "Narrated Rafi' bin Khadij:that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \"Whoever farms a people's land without their permission, then nothing he farms belongs to him and its finances are due to him",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-15-1366-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-15-1366-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-15-1366-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Daif"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c745dd1a4c9c86f0b77b",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 15,
      "hadithIndex": 1367,
      "bookHadithIndex": 48,
      "text": "Narrated An-Nu'man bin Bashir:That his father gave a slave to a son of his. So he went to the Prophet (ﷺ) to have him witness it. He (ﷺ) said: 'Have you given a gift similar to this one to all of your sons?' He replied: 'No'. So he said: 'Then take him back",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-15-1367-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-15-1367-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-15-1367-basharawadmaarouf",
          "name": "Bashar Awad Maarouf",
          "grade": "Hasan Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-15-1367-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih - Agreed Upon"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c745dd1a4c9c86f0b77c",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 15,
      "hadithIndex": 1368,
      "bookHadithIndex": 49,
      "text": "Narrated Samurah:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \"The neighbor of a home has more right to the home",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-15-1368-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-15-1368-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-15-1368-basharawadmaarouf",
          "name": "Bashar Awad Maarouf",
          "grade": "Hasan Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-15-1368-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Hasan"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c745dd1a4c9c86f0b77d",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 15,
      "hadithIndex": 1369,
      "bookHadithIndex": 50,
      "text": "Narrated Jabir:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \"The neighbor has more right to his preemption. He is to be waited for even if he is absent, when their paths are the same",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-15-1369-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-15-1369-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-15-1369-basharawadmaarouf",
          "name": "Bashar Awad Maarouf",
          "grade": "Hasan"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-15-1369-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Isnaad Hasan"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c745dd1a4c9c86f0b77e",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 15,
      "hadithIndex": 1370,
      "bookHadithIndex": 51,
      "text": "Narrated Jabir bin 'Abdullah:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \"When the boundaries are defined and the streets are fixed, then there is no preemption",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-15-1370-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-15-1370-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-15-1370-basharawadmaarouf",
          "name": "Bashar Awad Maarouf",
          "grade": "Hasan Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-15-1370-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih Bukhari"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c745dd1a4c9c86f0b77f",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 15,
      "hadithIndex": 1371,
      "bookHadithIndex": 52,
      "text": "Narrated Ibn Abbas:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \"The partner is the preemptor, and preemption is in everything",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-15-1371-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Daif Munkar"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-15-1371-alalbani",
